Z||000007||Shiner||01-05-2001||01:05 AM||||I was worried I had some frame damage on the GT, because I know it has been hit before, and the door hung very low and took a good slam to close properly.  Most of the door was pretty trashed, so we swapped the SE's door onto the GT.  With the bolts semi-loose, the trick was to get INSIDE the car, have somebody close you in there, and tighten that bolt that goes from the inside of the car, under the dash.  We opened the door, I got out, and we closed it.  It was beautiful  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>------------------<BR>-Shiner-<BR>'84 Sport Coupe<BR>'87 GT<BR>'86 SE 2M6 (parts car)||||reg||1
